0..110 Comment "/// This source checks pairs against definitions whose dependent record types reach a record type over a call."
111..114 Comment "///"
115..244 Comment "/// It pins the kernel\'s replay of those definitions\' unfoldings, which relates the kernel\'s own δ-step to the checker\'s reduct."
245..248 Comment "///"
249..496 Comment "/// Each record type is reached through an arm stuck on the outer record\'s first field. The checker\'s reduct runs the call inside the record type. The kernel\'s δ-step holds it, and the kernel reads the two codes alike once their decodes are read."
497..500 Comment "///"
501..517 Comment "/// - see: #3045"
518..534 Comment "/// - see: #2831"
